      'routing_direct': 'DIRECT',
      'routing_changes': '{count} CHANGES',
      'routing_duration': 'Duration: {duration}',
      'routing_origin_hint': 'Where from? (e.g. Rome)',
      'routing_destination_hint': 'Where to? (e.g. Milan)',
      'routing_search_btn': 'Search Routes',
      'routing_empty': 'Enter your origin and destination to find the best routes.',
      'routing_no_results': 'No solutions found between these stations.',
      'routing_time_now': 'Now',
      'routing_time_label': 'Time',
      'routing_time_date_label': 'Date',
      
      // --- Onboarding ---
      'onboarding_welcome': 'Welcome to BC.TRANSPORTER',
      'onboarding_subtitle': 'To continue, please read and accept the Privacy Policy and License Terms (EULA).',
      'onboarding_privacy_prefix': 'I have read and accept the ',
      'onboarding_privacy_link': 'Privacy Policy',
      'onboarding_privacy_text': 'PRIVACY POLICY\nBC.TRANSPORTER\nLast updated: September 2026\nVersion 1.0\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\nINTRODUCTION — WHAT IS BC.TRANSPORTER\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\nBC.TRANSPORTER is a multi-modal mobile application that integrates into a single platform the real-time monitoring of:\n\n• Buses, divided into Urban (city lines such as AMTAB Bari, TPER Emilia-Romagna, GTT Turin: stops on the map and waiting times) and Extra-urban and national (such as Flixbus: routes, timetables and journey times).\n• Trains, divided into National (boards for Italy, France, Germany, Switzerland, Austria: departures/arrivals, delays, platforms) and Regional (operators such as Trenord, FAL, FSE, Ferrotramviaria: stations, departures/arrivals, trip details and alerts).\n• Flights (via FlightRadar integration): live airspace radar, departures and arrivals by ICAO/IATA airport code.\n• Weather: atmospheric conditions for the selected city.\n\nThe app also allows: saving routes and stations in favourites, downloading offline data, receiving push notifications for delays and arrivals, sharing your live trip via link, planning rail itineraries, and accessing historical station statistics.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n1. DATA CONTROLLER\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\nThe data controller is the BC.TRANSPORTER development team. For any privacy-related request, please contact us through the app\'s official channels.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n2. DATA COLLECTED AND PURPOSES\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n2.1 GPS LOCATION\nThe app requests access to your geographic location. GPS is used exclusively to:\n- Show nearby transport on the interactive map;\n- Calculate distance from stops/stations;\n- Auto-detect your city for weather.\nYour location is NOT transmitted to third parties or stored on remote servers.\n\n2.2 ACCOUNT & AUTHENTICATION\nIf you register, your username and password are processed. Passwords are protected via bcrypt hashing (irreversible) and stored in a secure cloud database (Turso/LibSQL). Sessions are securely maintained between app restarts.\n\n2.3 FAVOURITES & SETTINGS\nData for saved stations, trains, language (Italian/English/German), theme (light/dark), auto-refresh intervals, and notification settings are stored locally on your device via SharedPreferences.\n\n2.4 OFFLINE DATA (LOCAL CACHE)\nFor offline use, the app downloads and stores locally — via SQLite — routes, timetables, stops, and line data. This data stays on your device and can be deleted from the app settings.\n\n2.5 LIVE TRIP SHARING\nWhen you use "Share Live Trip", a temporary link is generated (e.g. betacloud-transporter.is-cool.dev/share?id=...) containing information about your current trip (train number, route, estimated position). The link has an automatic expiry and data is removed from the server upon expiry.\n\n2.6 PUSH NOTIFICATIONS\nThe app can send notifications on Android and iOS for: delay or cancellation alerts for monitored trains, approaching stop alerts for your selected station. Required data (train ID, stop of interest) is managed via native OS background workers.\n\n2.7 WEATHER DATA\nYour city (entered manually or detected via GPS) is used to query an external weather service. No logs of these requests are stored.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n3. LEGAL BASIS\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n- Explicit consent (Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR) for GPS, notifications, and account.\n- Legitimate interest (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR) for local cache required for offline functionality.\n- Contract performance (Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR) for account-related features.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n4. SHARING WITH THIRD PARTIES\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\nYour personal data is NOT sold or shared with third parties for commercial purposes. The app connects to the following external services solely to retrieve transport data:\n- BC.TRANSPORTER server (betacloud-transporter.is-cool.dev): bus, train, flight data, provider config.\n- Rail providers (RFI and national operators): real-time timetable data.\n- OpenStreetMap / flutter_map: geographic map rendering.\n- External weather services: atmospheric data.\n- Turso (LibSQL): cloud database for accounts and user sessions (encrypted connection).\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n5. DATA RETENTION\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n- Local data (favourites, settings, offline cache): retained on the device until the app is uninstalled or manually cleared.\n- Cloud account: retained until deletion is requested.\n- Trip sharing links: automatic server-side expiry.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n6. SECURITY\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n- Passwords encrypted with bcrypt (irreversible hashing).\n- All server communications via HTTPS.\n- Sessions managed securely with session tokens.\n- Local data is not file-encrypted (non-sensitive data only).\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n7. YOUR RIGHTS (GDPR)\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\nYou have the right to:\n- Access your personal data.\n- Rectify inaccurate data.\n- Delete your account and data.\n- Restrict processing.\n- Data portability.\n- Object to processing.\n\nYou can exercise these rights directly from the app Settings or by contacting the development team.\n\nYou also have the right to lodge a complaint with the competent supervisory authority (in Italy, the Garante per la protezione dei dati personali: www.garanteprivacy.it).\n\nLegal texts online:\n- EU Regulation 2016/679 (GDPR): https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2016/679/oj\n- Italian Data Protection Authority: https://www.garanteprivacy.it\n- EU consumer rights: https://europa.eu/youreurope/citizens/consumers/index_en.htm\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n8. CHILDREN\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\nThis app is not intended for children under 13. We do not knowingly collect data from minors.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n9. CHANGES TO THIS POLICY\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\nWe reserve the right to update this policy. Significant changes will be notified at app startup. Continued use after notification constitutes acceptance of the changes.',
      'onboarding_eula_prefix': 'I have read and accept the ',
      'onboarding_eula_link': 'EULA',
      'onboarding_eula_text': 'END USER LICENSE AGREEMENT (EULA)\nBC.TRANSPORTER\nLast updated: September 2026\nVersion 1.0\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\nARTICLE 1 — ACCEPTANCE OF TERMS\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\nBy downloading, installing or using BC.TRANSPORTER, you fully accept the terms of this agreement. If you do not accept these terms, you may not install or use the app.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\nARTICLE 2 — DESCRIPTION OF THE APPLICATION\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\nBC.TRANSPORTER is a Flutter-based mobile app that integrates:\n\nREAL-TIME BUSES\nLive monitoring of urban and long-distance buses for: AMTAB (Bari), TPER (Emilia-Romagna), GTT (Turin), Flixbus. Shows real-time GPS positions, routes on the map, estimated arrival times, and delay alerts.\n\nREAL-TIME TRAINS\nLive departure/arrival board for stations in Italy, France, Germany, Switzerland, Austria and regional operators (including FAL - Ferrovie Appulo Lucane). Features: full trip stop details, scheduled vs. estimated times, platform changes, service alerts, historical statistics per station and per train.\n\nFLIGHTS — AIR RADAR\nReal-time air traffic radar via FlightRadar integration. View live flights, departures and arrivals for any airport by ICAO or IATA code, with technical data (altitude, speed, heading).\n\nINTERACTIVE MAP\nOpenStreetMap-based map (flutter_map) showing buses, trains, stops, stations, and user position. Multiple map styles supported (streets, satellite, dark, light, custom).\n\nROUTE PLANNING\nRail itinerary search between stations with solutions, connections, duration, and train details.\n\nOFFLINE SYNC\nLocal cache engine (SQLite) storing routes, timetables, and line data for use without internet. Auto-sync when connectivity is restored.\n\nPUSH NOTIFICATIONS\nBackground workers (Android) for proactive train and stop monitoring. Notifications for: approaching stop alert (configurable 5–20 minutes), delays, cancellations, train/bus status updates.\n\nLIVE TRIP SHARING\n"Share Trip" feature generating a temporary link to share your real-time journey status with others.\n\nACCOUNT & FAVOURITES\nAuthentication system with personal account. Save stations, trains, and lines in favourites with cloud sync.\n\nWEATHER\nCurrent weather conditions for your reference city.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\nARTICLE 3 — LICENSE GRANTED\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\nYou are granted a personal, non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable license to use BC.TRANSPORTER on devices you own, solely for personal, non-commercial purposes.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\nARTICLE 4 — RESTRICTIONS\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\nYou may not:\n- Modify, decompile, disassemble or attempt to extract the source code.\n- Use the app for commercial, illegal, or harmful purposes.\n- Bypass or disable security measures.\n- Sell, sublicense, rent, or redistribute the app or any part of it.\n- Scrape or make unauthorized automated requests to APIs used by the app.\n- Create fake accounts or use the app for fraudulent activities.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\nARTICLE 5 — DISCLAIMER OF WARRANTIES\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\nIMPORTANT: BC.TRANSPORTER DOES NOT REPLACE THE OFFICIAL CHANNELS of transport companies (Trenitalia, Italo, FS, RFI, AMTAB, TPER, GTT, Flixbus, airlines, and others).\n\nData provided by the app — timetables, delays, positions, availability — is purely INFORMATIONAL and is obtained from third-party sources. BC.TRANSPORTER does not guarantee:\n- Accuracy, completeness, or timeliness of transport data.\n- Service continuity or absence of interruptions.\n- Correspondence between displayed data and actual transport conditions.\n\nFOR TICKET PURCHASES, AVAILABILITY, TRAVEL CONDITIONS AND OFFICIAL CONFIRMATIONS, ALWAYS USE THE OFFICIAL CHANNELS OF TRANSPORT COMPANIES (official websites, official apps, ticket offices, authorized agencies).\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\nARTICLE 6 — LIMITATION OF LIABILITY\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\nTo the maximum extent permitted by law, BC.TRANSPORTER is not liable for:\n- Missing a transport due to inaccurate or delayed information.\n- Financial damages arising from app use (e.g. wrong tickets, missed connections).\n- Service interruptions due to maintenance or technical issues.\n- Loss of locally stored data on the device.\n- Purchases made through unofficial channels based on app information.\n- Push notification failures due to the device OS.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\nARTICLE 7 — INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\nAll intellectual property rights in BC.TRANSPORTER (source code, design, graphics, name, logo) belong to the BC.TRANSPORTER development team.\n\nLogos, trademarks, and names of third-party transport companies (national and regional rail operators such as Trenitalia, Italo, Trenord, FAL, FSE, Ferrotramviaria, urban transit agencies such as AMTAB, TPER, GTT, long-distance carriers such as Flixbus, airlines, motorway concession companies, etc.) belong to their respective owners and are shown in the app for informational purposes only, without implying any affiliation, sponsorship, or endorsement.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\nARTICLE 8 — THIRD-PARTY SERVICES\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\nThe app integrates with third-party services:\n- Rail and public transport data providers.\n- OpenStreetMap for map rendering.\n- FlightRadar for air traffic data.\n- Turso (LibSQL) for cloud database.\n- Weather services for atmospheric forecasts.\n\nUse of these services is subject to their respective terms. BC.TRANSPORTER is not responsible for their availability or functionality.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\nARTICLE 9 — UPDATES AND CHANGES\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\nWe reserve the right to: update, modify, or improve the app at any time; modify these terms with notification at next app startup; suspend or discontinue the service, in whole or in part.\n\nTransport providers (railway operators, bus lines, airlines and their routes, timetables and logos) are added and updated automatically remotely, without needing to update the app: availability of individual providers may therefore vary over time.\n\nContinued use after notification of changes constitutes acceptance of the new terms.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\nARTICLE 10 — TERMINATION\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\nThe license terminates automatically upon violation of these terms. Upon termination, you must immediately cease using the app and uninstall it from your device.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\nARTICLE 11 — GOVERNING LAW\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\nThis agreement is governed by Italian law and applicable European regulations (including EU Regulation 2016/679 on data protection and EU consumer protection law). Any disputes shall be subject to the jurisdiction of the service provider\'s court, unless applicable consumer protection law provides otherwise.\n\nTexts online: EU Regulation 2016/679 https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2016/679/oj | EU consumer rights https://europa.eu/youreurope/citizens/consumers/index_en.htm',
